  "label": "Christian Bale is mapped as a 'Christian driver' who is horrible at driving",
  "description": "The text 'ever notice christians are horrible drivers' creates an analogical mapping where Christian Bale, as a known Christian actor, is implicitly projected as a representative of 'Christians' who are stereotyped as 'horrible drivers'. The visual of him posing next to the Batmobile (a complex vehicle requiring advanced driving skills) reinforces the stereotype by juxtaposing his identity with the implied incompetence of driving such a vehicle. This mapping relies on the viewer's knowledge of Bale's religious identity and the stereotype about Christians being bad drivers.",
